@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Tabs}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Usage}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Tabs @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Tabs @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</h1>

<p>
    Practical examples showing the Tabs component configured with various parameters.
</p>


<p>
    The example belows uses the two-way binding syntax to bind the variable <span class="code-span">_tabindex</span> to the <span class="code-span">ActiveTabIndex</span> parameter 
    and links to the id of the heading for its accessible name using via the <span class="code-span">AriaLabelledBy</span>. As the <span class="code-span">AutoActivatePane</span>
    parameter has been set to true, the tab panel will be shown when the recieves the focus when using the <kbd>Left Arrow</kbd> or <kbd>Right Arrow</kbd> keys.
</p>


<CodeBox CodeBlock="@TabsSnippets.Tabs_Setting_Parameters_Example" AriaLabel="Tabs setting paramaters code example" />

<p>
    The result of the parameter settings. The Tabs component is inside a section, the tabs component itself does not have border, the border is from the section element.
</p>

<section class="section-box" style="margin-top:var(--br-unit-space-7);">
    <h2 id="lifestyle-tabs">Lifestyle Tabs</h2>
    <Tabs @bind-ActiveTabIndex="_tabindex" AriaLabelledBy="lifestyle-tabs" AutoActivatePanel="true" TabIconPosition="TabIconPosition.Left" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <Tab TabTitle="Food" SvgIcon="--svg-food-icon" HasPanelTabIndex="true" PersistContent="true">
            <TabPanelContent>
                <h3>Recipes</h3>
                <p>
                    Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Proin sit amet sem vulputate, interdum justo vitae, sagittis nulla. Ut lectus augue, consectetur ut massa id,
                    tristique luctus eros. Donec tempus augue velit, vel vehicula tellus consequat vel. Integer tristique sem ac nisi sodales placerat. Integer nulla ex, tincidunt ut
                    eleifend ut, vestibulum vel leo. Proin diam urna, finibus porttitor purus nec, tristique varius justo. Nunc vel dui sed dui elementum facilisis. Curabitur ac fermentum
                    urna. Integer vestibulum fermentum massa, quis auctor elit viverra eget.
                </p>
            </TabPanelContent>
        </Tab>
        <Tab TabTitle="Travel" SvgIcon="--svg-airplane-icon" HasPanelTabIndex="true" PersistContent="true">

            <TabPanelContent>
                <h3>Itinerary</h3>
                <p>
                    Nulla eu est lacus. Mauris sodales tortor in sem viverra porta. Nam in dapibus massa. Vivamus et augue quis mauris luctus pretium eu eu dolor. Maecenas gravida nisl non
                    ante facilisis, pulvinar vestibulum nibh sagittis. Pellentesque mollis sem at arcu mattis, id molestie augue cursus. Pellentesque dolor urna, ultricies quis iaculis ac,
                    rutrum luctus nulla. Integer et consequat erat. Sed eget metus in est pulvinar ultrices at nec lorem. Sed aliquam massa eget dui aliquet ullamcorper. Sed elit nisi, maximus
                    et erat molestie, bibendum rutrum diam. Phasellus cursus eleifend porta.
                </p>

            </TabPanelContent>
        </Tab>
        <Tab TabTitle="Exercise" SvgIcon="--svg-runner-icon" HasPanelTabIndex="true" PersistContent="true">

            <TabPanelContent>
                <h3>Workouts</h3>
                <p>
                    Mauris imperdiet nisi nec pulvinar porta. Sed semper viverra venenatis. Sed accumsan, erat condimentum ornare malesuada, erat mauris tincidunt enim, non interdum quam sem
                    ac velit. Nunc et enim lorem. Maecenas gravida tortor eget ligula efficitur ullamcorper. Cras ut nisi elementum, maximus ante eu, vestibulum nibh. Vestibulum nec iaculis elit,
                    sit amet sagittis ex.
                </p>
            </TabPanelContent>
        </Tab>
    </Tabs>
</section>
<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong>If you know that the panel content contains any focusable elements then you should set the <span class="">PersistContent</span> parameter to false so if the user presses the 
    <kbd>Tab</kbd> key focus is moved to the first focusable element.
</p>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Tabs}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Api}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Tabs - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Toggletip}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Toggletip - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>
@code {

    private int _tabindex = 0;

}